    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Alison Benson, a childhood victim of sexual abuse, grew up with a psychosomatic condition that left her unable to feel touch, taste, or smell, experiencing life as a distant, hollow dream. Her search for sensation led through self-mutilation, drugs, S&amp;M and eventually torture and murder; she was Embraced by an unknown sire on the night before her sentencing for killing five lovers, and tore her own sire apart in ecstatic frenzy upon rising, savoring physical sensation for the first time. She rebuilt the burned-out lair of Montreal's original Cathari coven, the Widows, in the late 1950s, using the flesh of lured victims, and now leads the reborn coven from &quot;The Heart,&quot; Montreal's most notorious den of dark pleasure. She was named the city's third bishop under Archbishop Sangris.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>You are neither man nor woman but both, using your androgyny to keep others off balance. Your voice fluctuates from male to female and is known to leave Toreador antitribu transfixed. Only passion, desire, experience and degradation matter to you.</p><h2>Secrets</h2><p>The Rose and the Widows know a great deal of what happens in Montreal, learned largely from the Shepherds who visit them on their dark cycles.</p>",
    "notes": "Embraced 1957. Apparent age: early 20s. Uses Vicissitude on herself constantly, never appearing quite the same twice. Path of Cathari 10. Disciplines (as printed): Auspex 4, Celerity 2, Dominate 4, Presence 5, Vicissitude 5.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
